title: "bdd-specification-drift: replication package for a mutation-based instrument for detecting executable-specification drift in Cucumber-style suites"
type: software
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-11-25"
license: MIT
authors:
  - given-names: "João"
    family-names: "Correia de Brito"
    email: "correiadebrito.joao@gmail.com"
    orcid: ""
repository-code: "https://github.com/jcorreiabrito/bdd-specification-drift"
keywords:
  - behaviour-driven development
  - BDD
  - Cucumber
  - Gherkin
  - mutation testing
  - test oracle
  - specification drift
  - empirical software engineering
  - design science research
abstract: >-
  Replication package for a study that builds and evaluates a mutation-based instrument
  for measuring the oracle strength of BDD (Cucumber) specification layers, tests its
  feasibility in the Java (PIT) and JavaScript/TypeScript (Stryker) ecosystems, and
  applies it to a pre-registered frame of 2,552 public repositories. Contains the frame
  enumeration with snapshot hash and sampling seed, the screening and attrition tables,
  the static-indicator and mutation harnesses with pinned tool versions, the raw
  per-mutant statuses, the analysis scripts, and an append-only run log.
references:
  - type: article
    title: "Do Public BDD Suites Still Work as Oracles? A Mutation-Based Instrument for Detecting Executable-Specification Drift in Cucumber-Style Suites"
